The attribute supports the following argument types:

- `string` : returns the header value as a string;
- `array` : returns the header values as an array. For the `accept` , `accept-charset` , `accept-language` and `accept-encoding` headers, the values are automatically parsed (e.g. `accept-language: en-us,en;q=0.5` returns `['en_US', 'en']` );
- [AcceptHeader](https://github.com/symfony/symfony/blob/8.1/src/Symfony/Component/HttpFoundation/AcceptHeader.php) : returns a parsed `AcceptHeader` object for advanced quality-value handling.

If the header is missing and the argument has no default value and is not

