When using public properties, context is not supported. In order to support it,

you must declare a setter to write your property:

```
// src/Entity/BlogPost.php
namespace App \ Entity ; class BlogPost
{ public string $ currentPlace ; // ... public function setCurrentPlace ( string $ currentPlace , array $ context = []) : void { // assign the property and do something with the context }
}
```

Note

The marking store type could be "multiple\_state" or "single\_state". A single

state marking store does not support a model being on multiple places at the

same time. This means a "workflow" must use a "multiple\_state" marking store

and a "state\_machine" must use a "single\_state" marking store. Symfony

